<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Basic Commands on STEP Batch 12</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/tags/basic-commands/</link><description>Recent content in Basic Commands on STEP Batch 12</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en_US</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:59:00 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://step-12.github.io/tags/basic-commands/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Git basic commands</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/intro_git/git_basics/</link><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/intro_git/git_basics/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;In the previous post, you used &lt;code&gt;gacp&lt;/code&gt; to send your changes to GitHub, without worrying about what it does.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Time to look inside.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The name gives it away:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;gacp&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; │││└─ push&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; ││└── commit&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; │└─── add&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; └──── git&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;gacp&lt;/code&gt; runs &lt;strong&gt;add&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;commit&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;push&lt;/strong&gt; for you, one after the other.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In this post, we will go through each of them by hand.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="the-loop"&gt;The loop&lt;a class="anchor" href="#the-loop"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Every time you change your code, you go through the same loop:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>